      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SMALL MERCIES (2) has some solid form under her belt and proved too classy last time to win by 2.75 lengths at this track in a handy 22.52 beating SIMPKIN. Expected to be right there at the finish again. JUST QUICKLY (4) turned in a plain effort last time when seventh at this track over 390m behind Master Woods (22.63) in a Grade 4/5. Has ability and can measure up. MONARCH (1) jumped from out wide and was game in defeat last start when a 0.8 lengths third (24.46) behind Peaky Collinda at Bendigo. Has performed well from this box with a win and three minor placings to her name from five starts. Expected to be in the finish again. SIMPKIN (8) placed last time and is worth some thought.",
